to extract the second byte from the left,
	value >> 16 & 0xff

/16 for subnet mask: 255.255.0.0

Convert /24 to a subnet mask(value)
	(0xFFFFFFFF << (32 - prefix)) & 0xFFFFFFFF
	since python follows random precision integer arithmetic.

Get the host from the given IP and subnet mask
	IP & mask => subnet number.
